{"sha":"0d5823465d5ce9add526b227e2f98eb8d70dc17c","node_id":"C_kwDOTDJ7sdoAKDBkNTgyMzQ2NWQ1Y2U5YWRkNTI2YjIyN2UyZjk4ZWI4ZDcwZGMxN2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Scormave","email":"5045197+Scormave@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-02T15:58:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"Scormave","email":"5045197+Scormave@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-02T15:58:00Z"},"message":"feat: Find people entered twice with find_duplicates

find_duplicates is a new read-only tool (35 tools). It reads every
person of the tree with their profile, 500 per request and up to
20000 people, and lists the pairs that may be one person: possible
duplicates first, then similar pairs by how close the births are,
numbered across pages. Each person shows the Gramps ID, handle,
birth, death and parents, and the reply names get_object and
merge_objects as the next steps. personHandle and surname narrow the
pairs; limit and offset page through them. A tree that grows while
it is read gets a note that the pairs with the others are not shown.

The pairs come from the comparison of the create check, now one
Compare that both share. Names compare across spellings and the male
and female forms of a surname, alternate names count, and a pair of
the other gender, with other patronymics, born or dead more than five
years apart, or where one died before the other was born, is someone
else. People with a patronymic but no surname pair by given name and
patronymic, and only when their birth years or parents compare.
Spouses, and a person and their parent, grandparent or earlier
ancestor, are never paired: Gramps refuses to merge spouses or a
parent with their child, and a namesake grandfather is someone else.

Given names are the same when the first word of one is a word of the
other: Мария and Анна Мария, but not Robert de and Gilbert de, or
Иван Петрович and Петр Петрович. The create check of create_person
and create_records follows the same rule, and drops a namesake who
died before the new person's birth year.

The server instructions, README, docs, MCPB manifest and site list
the new tool. The create-check integration test now builds its
surname with -ov, so that adding -a gives a female form the check
knows.

The tests and comments now use the made-up surname Образцов, and the
tool descriptions and catalog name no Russian surname: the male and
female forms are Kowalski and Kowalska and the endings -ов and -ова.

Unit tests cover the given-name rule, the death years, the scan with
its filters, paging and exclusions, and the reply; an integration
test lists a person entered twice but not a namesake who died before
the other was born. Tried on demo.grampsweb.org: 2211 of 4675 people
compared (the others have the whole name in the given name), 13
possible duplicates and 103 similar pairs, down from 24 and 623
before the given-name rule, the ancestors and the death years; the
reading takes 13 to 20 seconds.","tree":{"sha":"629a7fd614a380548eb788cece12c70d21543b9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/git/trees/629a7fd614a380548eb788cece12c70d21543b9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/git/commits/0d5823465d5ce9add526b227e2f98eb8d70dc17c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commits/0d5823465d5ce9add526b227e2f98eb8d70dc17c","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commit/0d5823465d5ce9add526b227e2f98eb8d70dc17c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commits/0d5823465d5ce9add526b227e2f98eb8d70dc17c/comments","author":{"login":"Scormave","id":5045197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDUxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5045197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"Scormave","id":5045197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDUxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5045197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave","followers_url":"https://ap